  message: "NOT YET CLOSEABLE (correction to the 2026-07-10 F1 note's fold assumption). Three sub-metas now resolved: INV-fivar (sub-A) satisfied, INV-pikob (sub-B) satisfied, INV-rugah (sub-C) satisfied this pass. WI-pofas folded (true duplicate: empty body + shared dogfood_anon_id ITEM-e5ca58). BUT WI-gogif's OWN stated expectation — 'Read subcommands should follow one consistent convention for JSON output (such as a --format text|json flag pair)' — is measurably UNMET: io-boundaries + verify-claims still expose --json (not --format json), slice uses --flat. WI-kitud captures this residual flag-spelling gap precisely — verified NOT a duplicate (see its updated entry; the prior scoping's 'fold WI-kitud as F1 dup' was falsified by the flag audit). Closing WI-gogif now would false-satisfy against its statement (INV-nufob-style). Envelope contract (F1 add_schema_envelope) + JSON-availability (INV-fivar) + wire-format documentation (INV-rugah) are all DONE; only flag-spelling uniformity (WI-kitud) remains. WI-gogif closes when WI-kitud closes."  # 0e94
